Title: Coffee Break
Credit: Written by
Author: Jack Gilmore
Description: An example one-scene comedy sketch, the simplest kind of script.
Draft date: 2026-10-08
Revision: Second Draft

INT. OFFICE BREAK ROOM - DAY

A coffee machine. It is enormous, chrome, and has far too many buttons.

SAM (30s) stares at it. PRIYA (30s) enters with a mug.

PRIYA
You've been here twenty minutes.

SAM
It asked me a question.

PRIYA
It's a coffee machine.

SAM
It asked me how I *feel*.

Priya leans over. The screen reads: HOW ARE YOU TODAY? She presses a button. The machine whirs and pours a perfect cup.

PRIYA
You press "fine." You always press "fine."

SAM
(taking the coffee, shaken)
I wasn't fine, though.

PRIYA
Nobody's fine. That's why there's coffee.

She leaves. Sam looks at the machine. The machine looks at Sam.

SMASH CUT TO:

INT. OFFICE BREAK ROOM - LATER

Sam and the coffee machine. Sam is sitting on the counter now, talking with his hands.

SAM
...and that's when I realized I'd never actually *liked* jazz.
